514 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Succeeding from the Inner Self)
/E (Succeeding from the Inner Self)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
515 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (All true success flows from inside out. Success and greatness is more as a result of internal attributes than external conditions. This is the reason that two people can have exact external circumstances from birth till adulthood and turn out with life outcomes as different as the North pole from the South. It is a fact that two people can be born in the same location, by the same parents, go to the same schools, taught by the same teachers and one turns out a failure and the other a success. Whenever this happens, then there is necessarily somewhere along the life journey of such people that one must have got access to certain information, people, event or things that conditioned his/her inner realities differently from the other. If we carefully review the lives of such people, we would be able to somehow somewhere account for how the successful person made certain decisions or was exposed to certain environments, people, information or events that constructed his/her inner self differently from the failed people. The success or failure of each of these persons in our study must definitely have flowed from their inner realities.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
