524 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T ("Let us make man in our image, in our likeness . . . So God created man in his own image, in the image of God he created him; male and female he created them. )
/E ("Let us make man in our image, in our likeness . . . So God created man in his own image, in the image of God he created him; male and female he created them. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
525 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Humanity was made in the image and likeness of God - this truth is fundamental to self-discovery. Believing anything less puts one at risk of confusion. Primarily, being made in the image and likeness of God talks about the fact that man \(both male and female\) was created a spirit in the order and class of God. Thus, the God-nature, His DNA, is in man by creation. Furthermore, being made in the image and likeness of God implies that there is the revelation of God that is fabricated into the created man which he is to reveal on earth. Thus, there is something about God that every created person represents and is to reveal to the world. Self discovery is simply knowing the dimension of God that you were created to reveal to your world.)
/E (Humanity was made in the image and likeness of God - this truth is fundamental to self-discovery. Believing anything less puts one at risk of confusion. Primarily, being made in the image and likeness of God talks about the fact that man \(both male and female\) was created a spirit in the order and class of God. Thus, the God-nature, His DNA, is in man by creation. Furthermore, being made in the image and likeness of God implies that there is the revelation of God that is fabricated into the created man which he is to reveal on earth. Thus, there is something about God that every created person represents and is to reveal to the world. Self discovery is simply knowing the dimension of God that you were created to reveal to your world.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
