/ActualText (He had before this time declared who He was, but the claims He made about who He was did not go down well with some people. Even though, He knew who He was, He still wanted to know what perception of people about Him was. This was not so that He could get His self-identity or self-definition from their perception, but so that He could assertively correct the wrong perception about Him of people closest to Him. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [4]
