721 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (This understanding underscores the difference between career and assignment. While a career or ministry could be a vital platform for carrying out your assignment, it is not the assignment. Thus, becoming a doctor is not a life assignment or purpose, but believing you are sent by God to bring healing to the hurting through medicine is a life assignment. Being a political leader is not a life assignment, but knowing that you were created by God to bring integrity to the governance of a people, community or nation is a life assignment. Being a pastor or apostle is not a life assignment, but knowing that God has called you to get people saved and establish a local assembly where they will be nurtured to grow into all that God wants them to be is a life assignment. One could be a doctor and not fulfil his/her life assignment. One could be an apostle and be missing his/her life assignment. Your life assignment is to be thought about in terms of a task, message, and job description. Not a career path or a ministry appellation. )
/E (This understanding underscores the difference between career and assignment. While a career or ministry could be a vital platform for carrying out your assignment, it is not the assignment. Thus, becoming a doctor is not a life assignment or purpose, but believing you are sent by God to bring healing to the hurting through medicine is a life assignment. Being a political leader is not a life assignment, but knowing that you were created by God to bring integrity to the governance of a people, community or nation is a life assignment. Being a pastor or apostle is not a life assignment, but knowing that God has called you to get people saved and establish a local assembly where they will be nurtured to grow into all that God wants them to be is a life assignment. One could be a doctor and not fulfil his/her life assignment. One could be an apostle and be missing his/her life assignment. Your life assignment is to be thought about in terms of a task, message, and job description. Not a career path or a ministry appellation. )
/Pg 54 0 R
/K [4]
