<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (The kingdom of God does not refer to a church or religion, it is the governing influence of God over a territory, run by His principles, impacted with His will, purpose and intents, and producing a people who express His culture and reflect His nature. Thus, the Kingdom of God is used to describe any territory, place, person, system, organisation, business, or nation that is ruled under the recognition of the Lordship of the Person of Jesus, by the principles of the Word of God, and whose lives express a culture that depicts the character of God. An individual, family, business, enterprise, institution, ministry, political state, country, or territory can be the Kingdom of God. Thus, Luke 17: 20 - 21 records, now when He was asked by the Pharisees when the kingdom of God would come, He answered them and said, "The kingdom of God does not come with observation;  nor will they say,'See here!' or 'See there!' For indeed, the kingdom of God is within you."    Luke 17:20-21 NKJV.)
/E (The kingdom of God does not refer to a church or religion, it is the governing influence of God over a territory, run by His principles, impacted with His will, purpose and intents, and producing a people who express His culture and reflect His nature. Thus, the Kingdom of God is used to describe any territory, place, person, system, organisation, business, or nation that is ruled under the recognition of the Lordship of the Person of Jesus, by the principles of the Word of God, and whose lives express a culture that depicts the character of God. An individual, family, business, enterprise, institution, ministry, political state, country, or territory can be the Kingdom of God. Thus, Luke 17: 20 - 21 records, now when He was asked by the Pharisees when the kingdom of God would come, He answered them and said, "The kingdom of God does not come with observation;  nor will they say,'See here!' or 'See there!' For indeed, the kingdom of God is within you."    Luke 17:20-21 NKJV.)
/Pg 74 0 R
